<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  TEMPORARY — HealthKit is removed so a free Apple ID (Personal Team) can
	  provision a device build for camera testing. HealthKit is not in the
	  capability set free provisioning grants, and leaving it here fails the
	  build at provisioning rather than at compile time.

	  The build setting CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = Config/HeathFirst.entitlements
	  is deliberately left in place — losing it is the failure mode CLAUDE.md
	  warns about. Only the keys were taken out.

	  RESTORE before shipping, or as soon as a paid Developer Program account
	  is used, by putting these back:

	      <key>com.apple.developer.healthkit</key>
	      <true/>
	      <key>com.apple.developer.healthkit.access</key>
	      <array/>

	  Until then Apple Health reads fail on device and the onboarding screen
	  says "Apple Health hiện không khả dụng" — handled, not a crash.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
